1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,592
Nobody remembers the feedback. They
remember how it felt.

2
00:00:05,562 --> 00:00:07,341
So start with what you saw.

3
00:00:08,891 --> 00:00:11,769
Say what you saw. Say what it cost.

4
00:00:12,739 --> 00:00:16,327
Then ask what they meant, before you tell
them the fix.

5
00:00:17,877 --> 00:00:22,676
A judgement is about them. An observation
is about the work.

6
00:00:23,646 --> 00:00:25,801
Only one of the two can be fixed.

7
00:00:27,351 --> 00:00:33,081
Twenty percent observed. Thirty percent
impact. Fifty percent question.

8
00:00:34,051 --> 00:00:35,758
Let them answer first.

9
00:00:37,308 --> 00:00:42,058
One thing at a time. Two is a review, not
a conversation.

10
00:00:43,028 --> 00:00:45,258
Pick one thing, not five.

11
00:00:46,808 --> 00:00:52,243
Ask, then tell. Then try it reversed:
tell, then ask.

12
00:00:53,793 --> 00:00:58,634
Saw, cost, meant. Three sentences and a
question.

13
00:01:00,184 --> 00:01:03,490
Ask what they meant. Then say what you
saw.
